.","observation":"Water is present before dry land appears and is gathered into seas."},{"id":"genesis-7","reference":"Genesis 7:17–24","title":"Waters cover the earth","phase":"Flood","book":"Genesis","chapter":7,"excerpt":"The waters rose, and increased greatly on the earth.","observation":"Water that had boundaries in creation now overwhelms the dry ground."},{"id":"exodus-14","reference":"Exodus 14:21–22","title":"A path through the sea","phase":"Deliverance","book":"Exodus","chapter":14,"excerpt":"The waters were divided. The children of Israel went into the middle of the sea on the dry ground.","observation":"A blocked route becomes a passage; water stands on both sides of the crossing."},{"id":"exodus-17","reference":"Exodus 17:1–7","title":"Water from the rock","phase":"Provision","book":"Exodus","chapter":17,"excerpt":"Water will come out of it, that the people may drink.","observation":"In the wilderness, lack of water becomes a crisis of survival and trust."},{"id":"joshua-3","reference":"Joshua 3:15–17","title":"The Jordan stops","phase":"Threshold","book":"Joshua","chapter":3,"excerpt":"All Israel crossed over on dry ground, until all the nation had passed completely over the Jordan.","observation":"Another generation crosses water on dry ground as it enters the land."},{"id":"second-kings-5","reference":"2 Kings 5:10–14","title":"Naaman washes in the Jordan","phase":"Cleansing","book":"2 Kings","chapter":5,"excerpt":"Go and wash in the Jordan seven times.","observation":"The Jordan is not merely crossed; Naaman is instructed to enter it repeatedly and emerges clean."},{"id":"psalm-69","reference":"Psalm 69:1–3","title":"Deep water as distress","phase":"Distress","book":"Psalms","chapter":69,"excerpt":"The waters have come up to my neck!","observation":"Water becomes poetic language for being overwhelmed, not a travel scene or ritual action."},{"id":"ezekiel-47","reference":"Ezekiel 47:8–9","title":"A river brings life","phase":"Renewal","book":"Ezekiel","chapter":47,"excerpt":"Everything will live wherever the river comes.","observation":"Water flows outward from the temple and is associated with restored life."},{"id":"matthew-3","reference":"Matthew 3:13–17","title":"Jesus enters the Jordan","phase":"Baptism","book":"Matthew","chapter":3,"excerpt":"Jesus came from Galilee to the Jordan to John, to be baptized by him.","observation":"The Jordan becomes the setting for Jesus’ baptism and the beginning of his public ministry."},{"id":"john-4","reference":"John 4:10–14","title":"Living water at the well","phase":"Living water","book":"John","chapter":4,"excerpt":"The water that I will give him will become in him a well of water springing up to eternal life.","observation":"Ordinary well water becomes the starting point for a conversation about living water."},{"id":"revelation-22","reference":"Revelation 22:1–2","title":"The river of life","phase":"Completion","book":"Revelation","chapter":22,"excerpt":"He showed me a river of water of life, clear as crystal, proceeding out of the throne of God and of the Lamb.","observation":"The final vision returns to life-giving water alongside the tree of life."}],"dissects":[{"id":"water-dissect-genesis-1","passageId":"genesis-1"},{"id":"water-dissect-genesis-7","passageId":"genesis-7"},{"id":"exodus-14-crossing","passageId":"exodus-14"},{"id":"water-dissect-exodus-17","passageId":"exodus-17"},{"id":"water-dissect-joshua-3","passageId":"joshua-3"},{"id":"water-dissect-second-kings-5","passageId":"second-kings-5"},{"id":"psalm-69-deep-water","passageId":"psalm-69"},{"id":"ezekiel-47-river","passageId":"ezekiel-47"},{"id":"water-dissect-matthew-3","passageId":"matthew-3"},{"id":"water-dissect-john-4","passageId":"john-4"},{"id":"water-dissect-revelation-22","passageId":"revelation-22"}],"compares":[{"id":"two-crossings","pivotIds":["crossings","boundaries","beginnings"]},{"id":"creation-and-exodus","pivotIds":["beginnings","boundaries"]},{"id":"scene-and-metaphor","pivotIds":["